\details{
Outdoor ventilation retains the source minimum ACH time table.
A saved \code{OPTION.VARIANT_VENT = 0} disables the range supplement.
When the saved switch is absent, conversion retains its legacy
documented outdoor-temperature-band rule and warns about the assumed
enabled setting. The \code{ventilation} attribute records this selection.
A room group with \code{IS_AC_ROOM = 0} retains minimum ventilation only;
unused maximum and temperature-range references are not consumed.
In the default outdoor-band rule, the AC availability time table does
not gate the range increment. Explicit target prediction uses that
schedule in its own-state selection and supports intermediate flow.
The rule preserves the remaining range inputs
but does not reproduce DeST's internal ventilation control algorithm.
See \code{\link[=destep_opts]{destep_opts()}} for standalone target-state controls, their version
requirements and approximations; none consumes source simulation results.

Window-side surfaces stored with \code{OF_ROOM = -1} are restored from the
same side of their explicit \code{WINDOW.OF_ENCLOSURE} host. Restoration
requires unique references, an existing room/outdoor/ground owner and
no conflicting binding on the other side. Ambiguous or incomplete
relationships stop conversion. Only \code{OF_ROOM} and \code{TYPE} are restored;
geometry and thermal properties are retained. The default \code{copy = TRUE}
leaves the input database unchanged. A
\code{destep_restored_window_bindings} warning carries the affected records
in its \code{bindings} field. This restores redundant input relationships,
not missing geometry or DeST solver behavior.

Storey multipliers are mapped to ZoneGroup independently of source
surface boundaries. Outdoor, ground and interzone relationships are
retained. Interzone pairs with unequal multipliers produce a warning
and are listed in \code{conversion$surface_boundaries}: weighted outputs
must not be interpreted as a physically balanced whole-building model.
Successful conversion does not establish DeST thermal equivalence.
Missing enclosure-side or middle-plane references produce a
\code{destep_invalid_surface_references} error whose \code{references} table identifies
the source enclosure, field and saved reference.
